1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,521
This price says €9.99.

2
00:00:02,561 --> 00:00:04,240
Your brain reads nine.

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:05,510
But it's ten.

4
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:07,699
That's not an accident.

5
00:00:07,739 --> 00:00:08,972
Shops test prices,

6
00:00:09,012 --> 00:00:11,424
buttons and timers on millions of people.

7
00:00:11,464 --> 00:00:13,507
Your brain is the test subject.

8
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:15,529
Once you can see the tricks,

9
00:00:15,569 --> 00:00:17,233
most of them stop working.

10
00:00:17,933 --> 00:00:20,670
Here are seven of them, and how to beat each one.

11
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:24,496
One. The price that ends in nine.

12
00:00:25,067 --> 00:00:26,772
Your brain reads the first digit,

13
00:00:26,812 --> 00:00:28,362
and mostly stops there.

14
00:00:28,402 --> 00:00:32,118
So €9.99 feels much closer to nine than to ten.

15
00:00:32,833 --> 00:00:34,393
In one US experiment,

16
00:00:34,433 --> 00:00:36,205
a clothing catalogue raised the price

17
00:00:36,245 --> 00:00:39,899
of a dress from $34 to $39.

18
00:00:39,939 --> 00:00:41,858
It sold about a third more.

19
00:00:41,933 --> 00:00:45,727
At $44, it sold the same as at $34.

20
00:00:46,467 --> 00:00:49,384
The fix: round prices up in your head.

21
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:51,814
€9.99 is ten euros.

22
00:00:51,854 --> 00:00:54,221
€49.95 is fifty.

23
00:00:55,367 --> 00:00:57,242
Two. The decoy.

24
00:00:57,867 --> 00:01:00,332
A magazine once offered three options.

25
00:01:00,372 --> 00:01:01,634
Online only:

26
00:01:01,674 --> 00:01:03,272
$59.

27
00:01:03,312 --> 00:01:06,549
Print only: $125.

28
00:01:06,589 --> 00:01:07,967
Print and online:

29
00:01:08,007 --> 00:01:10,151
$125.

30
00:01:10,367 --> 00:01:12,247
Nobody picks print only.

31
00:01:12,287 --> 00:01:14,793
It's there to make the bundle look like a steal.

32
00:01:15,467 --> 00:01:17,177
In a famous class experiment,

33
00:01:17,217 --> 00:01:20,051
84% of students chose the bundle.

34
00:01:20,267 --> 00:01:21,717
When the decoy was removed,

35
00:01:21,757 --> 00:01:25,311
68% chose the cheap online option instead.

36
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:28,420
The fix: when you see three prices,

37
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:30,691
ask which one is only there to push you.

38
00:01:30,731 --> 00:01:32,527
Then compare the other two.

39
00:01:33,733 --> 00:01:36,136
Three. The fake countdown.

40
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:38,039
Only two left.

41
00:01:38,079 --> 00:01:40,040
Offer ends in ten minutes.

42
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:42,224
Someone in Paris just bought this.

43
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:43,961
Urgency switches off the slow,

44
00:01:44,001 --> 00:01:45,832
careful part of your brain.

45
00:01:46,533 --> 00:01:48,713
In a check published in 2023,

46
00:01:48,753 --> 00:01:53,573
EU consumer authorities looked at 399 online shops.

47
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:57,142
148 used at least one manipulative trick.

48
00:01:57,200 --> 00:02:00,378
42 of them had countdown timers that were fake.

49
00:02:01,067 --> 00:02:03,910
The fix: if a timer says hurry, wait.

50
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:06,319
A real deal survives a night of sleep.

51
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:09,578
Four. The fake discount.

52
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:12,569
Was €199.

53
00:02:12,609 --> 00:02:14,559
Now €99.

54
00:02:14,599 --> 00:02:15,851
Half price!

55
00:02:15,891 --> 00:02:19,029
But was it ever really €199?

56
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:21,350
A high before price is an anchor.

57
00:02:21,390 --> 00:02:23,545
It makes the new price feel small.

58
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:26,308
In the EU, since 2022,

59
00:02:26,348 --> 00:02:27,897
a shop announcing a discount has

60
00:02:27,937 --> 00:02:29,910
to compare it with its lowest price

61
00:02:29,950 --> 00:02:31,816
in the previous thirty days.

62
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,427
Here, that's €120.

63
00:02:34,467 --> 00:02:38,447
So the real discount is about 17%, not 50%.

64
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:40,820
Check that small line, or a price tracker,

65
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:42,748
before you believe the percentage.

66
00:02:43,867 --> 00:02:45,943
Five. Free shipping.

67
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:48,929
Shipping costs €4.90.

68
00:02:48,969 --> 00:02:50,971
It's free above €50.

69
00:02:51,011 --> 00:02:53,480
Your basket is at €38.

70
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:56,395
So you add a €15 thing you didn't plan to buy,

71
00:02:56,435 --> 00:02:58,479
to save €4.90.

72
00:02:59,067 --> 00:03:03,006
You just spent about €10 more to avoid paying €4.90.

73
00:03:03,167 --> 00:03:04,912
The fix: pay the shipping,

74
00:03:04,952 --> 00:03:07,173
or wait until you really need more.

75
00:03:08,167 --> 00:03:10,718
Six. Buy now, pay later.

76
00:03:11,300 --> 00:03:13,885
Four payments of €25 feel lighter

77
00:03:13,925 --> 00:03:16,193
than one payment of €100.

78
00:03:16,233 --> 00:03:18,281
It's the same €100.

79
00:03:18,533 --> 00:03:20,920
One large study of US bank data found

80
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:24,248
that once people start using buy now, pay later,

81
00:03:24,288 --> 00:03:25,913
their total spending goes up,

82
00:03:25,953 --> 00:03:27,483
and stays up for months.

83
00:03:28,267 --> 00:03:30,117
New EU consumer credit rules,

84
00:03:30,157 --> 00:03:33,122
applying from 20 November 2026,

85
00:03:33,162 --> 00:03:36,522
bring most buy now, pay later under credit law,

86
00:03:36,562 --> 00:03:38,831
with checks on whether you can afford it.

87
00:03:39,033 --> 00:03:41,383
The fix: if you can't pay for it today,

88
00:03:41,423 --> 00:03:43,513
you probably can't afford it today.

89
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:46,846
Seven. The store map.

90
00:03:47,533 --> 00:03:49,749
Milk and bread are usually at the back.

91
00:03:49,789 --> 00:03:52,395
To reach them, you walk past everything else.

92
00:03:52,633 --> 00:03:54,423
And the sweets wait at the checkout,

93
00:03:54,463 --> 00:03:57,098
right where you stand still with nothing to do.

94
00:03:57,667 --> 00:03:59,785
England even banned less healthy snacks

95
00:03:59,825 --> 00:04:03,200
from the checkouts of larger stores in 2022.

96
00:04:03,267 --> 00:04:04,120
The fix:

97
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,833
shop with a list, and walk straight to what's on it.

98
00:04:08,033 --> 00:04:09,462
Final message.

99
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:11,913
Some of these tricks are banned.

100
00:04:11,953 --> 00:04:13,807
Most are perfectly legal.

101
00:04:13,847 --> 00:04:15,889
They're just very good design.

102
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:18,069
Round prices up.

103
00:04:18,109 --> 00:04:19,589
Spot the decoy.

104
00:04:19,629 --> 00:04:21,046
Ignore the timer.

105
00:04:21,086 --> 00:04:22,913
Check the real old price.

106
00:04:22,953 --> 00:04:24,237
Pay the shipping.

107
00:04:24,277 --> 00:04:26,697
Pay in full. Bring a list.

108
00:04:27,367 --> 00:04:29,148
Your brain isn't stupid.

109
00:04:29,188 --> 00:04:30,296
It's just being tested

110
00:04:30,336 --> 00:04:32,134
by people who do this all day.

111
00:04:32,767 --> 00:04:35,622
This is education, not financial advice.

112
00:04:35,662 --> 00:04:37,430
If this helped, subscribe.

113
00:04:37,470 --> 00:04:41,305
Next up: how to save money so easily it feels illegal.
